Code Of Conduct

Recent changes have turned Github in a hostile working environment for Independant Game Designers.
Hard Requirements ( Zero Tolerance )

Do Not Assume because we met before that you have permission to change or alter my software if you're not part of my open source team. Or change features without consulting me.

Contribution Do not make changes unless I have personally vouched for you. Anyone doing this will be banned from this repository. This includes unauthorized changes to code of conduct, which is not a valid contribution.

Commercial And Non Academic Uses Do not repackage and rebrand this software to attempt to compete with it and provide no attribution.

Intellectual Property Do not submit AI Slop as contributions, or steal from other developers when submitting code in pull requests or in the issues panel. Or any other format where user-submissions are taken. This includes stealing my webcomic assets to sell them back to me.

Misuse Of Code Of Conduct Do not leverage or misuse these terms of service to justify repository take over and theft. People that do that will be blocked and reported to github immediatly.

Trans Issues Do not leverage or weaponize trans issues either for in a way not representative, or in despisal of, trans issues. This repository is not about this topic. I place this as low lier because one time is a mistake, two times is a pattern of bigotry.
